   "html_text": "Oresme’s interest and engagement in economic problems should not be seen as an isolated subject in his intellectual life. As Kaye (1998, 2) has argued, the preoccupation with measurement, gradation, and the quantification of qualities, so typical of Oresme and the natural philosophy of his period, was strongly influenced by the contemporary rapid monetization of European society.",
